= The Party School

The party grows faster than it can train its officials. District secretaries who joined last year are expected to explain imperialism, chair a strike committee and keep the accounts. [? if year <= 1920 : Hermann Duncker ?][? if year >= 1921 : Duncker and Thalheimer ?] want a proper school: three months in a rented villa for the best young workers of every district.

The first class would come back to the districts in the spring, and the Zentrale must decide what it learns.

- @classics: Marx, Engels and Luxemburg.
- @russia: The October insurrection.
- @practice: Union and works council practice.
- @easy_discard

@classics
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. In three months, graduates who argue for the Spartacist tradition.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; c_school_class = 1; c_school_due = time + 3

Young metalworkers read Capital at a long table, with Luxemburg's Accumulation open beside it.

@russia
